haskell-blackjack is a blackjack program written in haskell. 

The following project contains...
- Main.hs (haskell code portion)
- readme (description and compilation instructions)
- seed.txt (contains the current games seed) *MUST CONTAIN ONE INTEGER*
- test.txt (test cases documenting input/output)

The dealer draws until a 17, anything above a 21 is a bust. 

[Compilation Instructions]
- Download GHC (Glasgow Haskell Compiler) and cabal-install
  - (sudo apt install ghc cabal-install)
- Navigate to project directory
- cabal build
- caball run/cabal clean

if you wish to change the seed, alter seed.txt

[Limitations]

Lack of Tracking Bets
- There are no betting mechanics implemented in this program

Input Restrictions
- The user was required to input either 'hit' or 'stand', with zero whitespace
- Any other input will prompt the user to try again

Pseudo-Randomness
- The 'randomness' that occurs when shuffling the deck is not a true randomness
- can lead to predictability/tracking if the user knows the seed.

Manual Seed Management
- Incurring issues with files locking, the user is now required to manually alter seed.txt to change the seed.

No Support for Multiple Players


